hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17767","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr Abu Amir narrated to us who said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us who said: Qays ibn Bishr al-Taghlibi narrated to us who said: My father informed me, and he was a companion of Abu al-Darda, who said: In Damascus there was a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ibn al-Hanzaliyya, and he was a solitary man who rarely sat with people. He was only in prayer, and when he finished he only glorified and magnified Allah until he came to his family. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu al-Darda, and Abu al-Darda said to him: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and I came, then a man among them came and sat in the gathering in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, and said to a man beside him: If you had seen us when we met, we and the enemy, and so-and-so charged and thrust and said: Take it, and I am the Ghifari youth, what do you think of his saying. He said: I see nothing but that he has nullified his reward. Another heard that and said: I see no harm in that. They disputed until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard. He said: Glory be to Allah, there is no harm in being praised and rewarded. He said: I saw Abu al-Darda pleased with that, and he kept raising his head to him and saying: Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he would say: Yes. He kept repeating it to him until I would say he will surely kneel upon his knees."
"17768","He said: Then he passed by us another day, and Abu al-Darda said to him: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Spending upon horses in the path of Allah is like one who stretches his hand with charity without withholding it."
"17769","He said: Then he passed by us another day, and Abu al-Darda said to him: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a good man is Khuraym al-Asadi, were it not for the length of his hair and the trailing of his lower garment. That reached Khuraym, and he took a blade and cut his hair to the halves of his ears, and raised his lower garment to the halves of his shins. He said: My father informed me. He said: I entered upon Muawiya after that, and there was with him an old man whose hair was above his ears and whose cloak was to his shins. I asked about him, and they said: This is Khuraym al-Asadi."
"17770","He said: Then he passed by us another day while we were with Abu al-Darda, and Abu al-Darda said to him: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You are coming to your brothers, so set right your saddles and set right your garments, for Allah, Almighty and Majestic, does not love obscenity nor obscene speech."
"17771","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us who said: Muawiya, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Sulayman Abu al-Rabi. My father said: He is Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman from whom Shuba and Layth ibn Sad narrated, from al-Qasim the freedman of Muawiya who said: I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw people gathered and an old man relating to them. I said: Who is this. They said: Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyya. I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever eats meat, let him perform ablution."
"17772","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, Qays ibn Bishr al-Taghlibi narrated to me, from his father, and he was a companion of Abu al-Darda in Damascus, who said: In Damascus there was a man called Ibn al-Hanzaliyya, solitary, hardly speaking to anyone. He was only in prayer, and when he finished he glorified and magnified Allah and declared His oneness until he returned to his family. He said: One day he passed over us while we were with Abu al-Darda, and Abu al-Darda said to him: A word from you that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an expedition, and when we came, a man among them sat in a gathering in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, and said: O so-and-so, if you had seen so-and-so thrust then said: Take it, and I am the Ghifari youth, what do you think. He said: I see nothing but that his reward has been annulled. He said: They spoke about that until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard their voices and said: Rather, he is praised and rewarded. He said: Abu al-Darda was pleased with that until he was about to kneel upon his knees, and said: Did you hear it, repeatedly. He said: Yes."
"17773","Then he passed over us another day, and Abu al-Darda said: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What a good man is Khuraym al-Asadi, if he shortened his hair and shortened his lower garment. That reached Khuraym, so he hastened and took the blade and shortened of his hair, and raised his lower garment to the halves of his shins. My father said: I entered upon Muawiya and saw a man with him upon the couch, his hair above his ears, wrapped to the halves of his shins. I said: Who is this. They said: Khuraym al-Asadi."
"17774","He said: Then he passed over us another day, and Abu al-Darda said: A word from you that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: Yes, we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to us: You are coming to your brothers, so set right your saddles and your garments, until you are among the people as if you are a mole, for Allah, Almighty and Majestic, does not love obscenity nor obscene speech."
"17775","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me who said: Rabia ibn Yazid narrated to me, Abu Kabsha al-Saluli narrated to me that he heard Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyya al-Ansari, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Uyayna and al-Aqra asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for something, so he ordered Muawiya to write it for them. He did so, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sealed it and ordered it to be handed to them. As for Uyayna, he said: What is in it. He said: In it is what I was ordered. So he kissed it and tied it in his turban, and he was the wiser of the two men. And as for al-Aqra, he said: Shall I carry a document I do not know what is in it, like the document of al-Mutalammis. Muawiya told the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of their two sayings. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for a need and passed by a camel kneeling at the door of the mosque from the first of the day, then he passed by it at the end of the day while it was in its state. He said: Where is the owner of this camel. He was sought and not found. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear Allah concerning these beasts, then ride them sound and ride them fat, like one who is displeased just now. Whoever asks while he has what suffices him, he only increases himself of the fire of Hell. They said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and what suffices him. He said: What gives him lunch or gives him supper."
